{"D:\\wt\\smfuneral\\vlog\\smfuneral\\voz\\b002_t2.wav": {"text": "She had one rule, nobody sits down to eat until the family has eaten first. I thought she was being bossy. It took me years to understand that she was not being bossy at all. She was giving the family somewhere to be fed and she was giving the rest of us something to do with our hands. Here is the first lesson and the verse it comes from. It is from the sixth chapter of Galatians, the second verse. It says, bear ye one another's burdens and so fulfill the law of Christ. I used to read that as a nice thing to say at a funeral. Now I read it as a job description. When Harold died, the casseroles came for two weeks. Then the quiet came. Nobody means to forget. Life simply picks back up for everybody but you. I learned more about grief in the third month than I learned in the first two weeks.", "words": [{"w": " She", "s": 0.0, "e": 0.22}, {"w": " had", "s": 0.22, "e": 0.46}, {"w": " one", "s": 0.46, "e": 0.82}, {"w": " rule,", "s": 0.82, "e": 1.26}, {"w": " nobody", "s": 1.72, "e": 2.14}, {"w": " sits", "s": 2.14, "e": 2.54}, {"w": " down", "s": 2.54, "e": 2.88}, {"w": " to", "s": 2.88, "e": 3.1}, {"w": " eat", "s": 3.1, "e": 3.38}, {"w": " until", "s": 3.38, "e": 3.72}, {"w": " the", "s": 3.72, "e": 4.06}, {"w": " family", "s": 4.06, "e": 4.34}, {"w": " has", "s": 4.34, "e": 4.64}, {"w": " eaten", "s": 4.64, "e": 4.9}, {"w": " first.", "s": 4.9, "e": 5.5}, {"w": " I", "s": 5.92, "e": 6.14}, {"w": " thought", "s": 6.14, "e": 6.38}, {"w": " she", "s": 6.38, "e": 6.58}, {"w": " was", "s": 6.58, "e": 6.82}, {"w": " being", "s": 6.82, "e": 7.14}, {"w": " bossy.", "s": 7.14, "e": 7.8}, {"w": " It", "s": 8.0, "e": 8.22}, {"w": " took", "s": 8.22, "e": 8.42}, {"w": " me", "s": 8.42, "e": 8.7}, {"w": " years", "s": 8.7, "e": 9.02}, {"w": " to", "s": 9.02, "e": 9.36}, {"w": " understand", "s": 9.36, "e": 9.8}, {"w": " that", "s": 9.8, "e": 10.0}, {"w": " she", "s": 10.0, "e": 10.2}, {"w": " was", "s": 10.2, "e":